export const PRIVACY_HTML = "<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Privacy Policy, The Living Bread</title><link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://living-bread.org/legal/privacy\">\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"How The Living Bread collects, uses, shares, keeps and deletes personal data, including through AI assistants.\">\n<style>body{margin:0;background:#F8F5EE;color:#1d2a33;font:16px/1.65 Georgia,serif}main{max-width:720px;margin:0 auto;padding:40px 20px 80px}\nh1{font-size:32px;margin:0 0 6px}.u{font:600 12px/1 Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b7680}\n.i{font-style:italic;color:#3c4a54}h2{font-size:21px;margin:30px 0 8px}p{margin:0}a{color:#8a6a1f}</style></head>\n<body><main><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><div class=\"u\">The Living Bread \u00b7 Last updated October 7, 2026</div><p class=\"i\" style=\"margin-top:14px\">Your soul is not a data point. We collect as little as we can, we never sell it, and we hold what you share with care. Here is exactly how.</p><h2>What we collect</h2><p>Your account: email address and the name you choose, plus anything you add on purpose: photo, handle, bio, testimony, life verse, spiritual gifts, church, city, state, country, gender, birth year. Location only if you enable it, for the Kingdom map, nearby believers, and Refuge; approximate is enough, and off is allowed. What you create: posts, prayer requests, testimonies, serve offers and needs, bookings, storehouse items and asks, watches, community and church activity, and messages. A push token so notifications can reach this phone, removed when you sign out. The names in Bring Them Home are visible to your account alone.</p><h2>Why we use it</h2><p>We use what you give us for these purposes only: to run your account and sign you in; to show your posts, prayers and testimonies to the people you chose; to connect you with believers, churches, gatherings and Tables near you; to deliver the notifications you allowed; to keep the community safe through moderation, reports and abuse prevention; to fix crashes and keep the service working; and, with anonymous totals only, to understand which public pages help people. We never use your prayers, messages or anything you write for advertising, and we never sell or rent any of it.</p><h2>Religious belief is special data</h2><p>Because this is a Christian community, almost everything here reveals religious belief, which many laws, including the GDPR, treat as a special category of personal data. We process it only because you chose to share it, for the purpose you shared it for, and only with the audience you picked. You can withdraw that consent at any time by deleting the content or your account. We never infer your faith, your health or anything sensitive from how you use the app.</p><h2>What we deliberately never keep</h2><p>The Mercy Seat stores nothing you write, not on this phone and not on any server: the words dissolve. The Mirror keeps nothing unless you choose to save it to your own journal. Your streaks, Armor, Crossroads decisions, Family Covenant, and Path to Freedom markers live only on your device. Images and links in private messages are deleted after 24 hours. Angel words arrive without the sender\u2019s identity, and the record pairing angel and receiver is sealed from both.</p><h2>Simon and AI conversations</h2><p>Your conversation history with Simon is stored only on your device, never on our servers. So is anything you ask Simon to remember: those notes stay on your phone, you can see them by asking &quot;What do you remember about me?&quot;, and you can forget any of them, or all of them, at any time. To generate each reply, we send Anthropic, the AI provider: your message and a few recent lines; a short summary of your walk that the app builds on your device (your first name, the season you chose, and your standing prayer need if you set one); open requests you can already see in the app, by first name and city, so Simon can tell you who might need you; and up to three of your remembered notes that relate to your message. Under the API terms we use, that content is not used to train AI models. We do not read, store, or profile your conversations, prayers, or confessions, and nothing you tell Simon is ever used for advertising or recommendations. When you ask Simon to help you share a prayer, it drafts from your own words; nothing is shared until you edit it, choose who sees it, and share it yourself.</p><h2>AI assistants and connectors</h2><p>The Living Bread can be connected to AI assistants such as ChatGPT, Claude and Cursor through our connector server at mcp.living-bread.org. Without signing in, an assistant reads only what is already public: Scripture from our stored text, verses for a need, our public pages, churches, gatherings and communities. If you sign in through the connector, you approve it on a consent screen that names the assistant and what it may read. It can then read, as you, what you could read yourself in the app: the prayers prayed over you, the prayers you gave, your circles, your gatherings and your invitations. The ChatGPT plugin is read only: it cannot post, pray, send, record, delete or change anything. In other assistants you may also allow small acts, such as saying Amen, which happen only when you ask in plain words. What the assistant reads is sent to that assistant&#x27;s provider (for example OpenAI or Anthropic) to answer you, under that provider&#x27;s own privacy policy. We store no conversation from any assistant and never ask an assistant for your chat history. We keep three things apart. Operational telemetry: for every tool call, on every connection, we count the minute, the tool, the name and version the assistant gives itself, a general category of what was sought (such as Scripture, prayer or church), whether it succeeded and how long it took, the country (and, on the public connection only, the city) our network reports, and a random code for that conversation that names nobody. It never holds your account, an IP address, or anything you gave a signed-in tool. Public questions: for public discovery tools only (such as a verse search, a church search or a question about the faith), the words of the question up to 200 characters with e-mail addresses and phone numbers removed, the tool, the hour and the assistant&#x27;s name, never linked to the conversation; we never keep the words you give a signed-in tool, a prayer for someone, your own religious background, or a name you ask about. First-party links: a link to living-bread.org in an answer carries a short random code, so that if you open it the app can count that open and the steps taken afterwards in the app, such as opening Scripture or joining a community; the code identifies the answer, never you. All of this is used only to keep the connector working and to learn where the Body of Christ can respond better; only our small launch team sees it, and only as totals. Raw telemetry and public questions are deleted automatically after 90 days; daily totals with no conversation in them may be kept longer. Your personal spiritual history, what you save in the app, is separate: only you see it, and you can delete it or your account at any time. Revoke an assistant at any time in that assistant&#x27;s settings or by signing out of the connector; the server honors the revocation immediately.</p><h2>Kingdom Witness and the accounts you connect</h2><p>In Kingdom Witness you may connect accounts you post from on other platforms, so you can see how far your witness traveled. Today those platforms are X, TikTok, YouTube, Instagram, Threads and Facebook (Pages you manage). Connecting asks each one only for permission to read, never to post, like, follow or message. Posting is a separate permission you may give from Share the Witness, one platform at a time (today Mastodon only). It lets The Living Bread post a status, with a photo if you add one, only at the moment you press send; it cannot read, follow, message or delete. That key stays on your device, never on our server, and you can stop it there, which asks the platform to revoke it. Every other platform opens its own share window with your words in it, and you post there yourself. If you add a photo to a post going to Mastodon or Pinterest, it is stored in your own folder at a public address so that platform can fetch it. If you keep the Living Bread link on a post, we count the visits, prayers and joins that come through it, never who they are. Your sign-in key for each account is kept on your device and passes through our server only for the moment of a reading. Posts you choose to follow in Kingdom Witness keep their aggregate totals (impressions, views, likes, comments, shares) and the audience breakdowns the platform itself reports in aggregate (such as countries, age ranges or gender, as percentages or counts) on our server, never who saw them, so you can watch them grow; they are deleted when you stop following them or delete your account. If you turn on &quot;Keep my reach up to date while I&#x27;m away&quot; for an account, we keep an encrypted, read-only key for that platform on our server to refresh those totals while you are away. It is encrypted with a key that is not stored in our database, it is never used to post, it is never shared, and it is deleted the moment you turn it off or disconnect that account. It is off by default and chosen for each account on its own. While it is on, we may send you at most one note a morning saying how far your testimony traveled in the night, which you can turn off in notification settings.</p><h2>Who processes data for us</h2><p>Supabase hosts our database, sign-in, and file storage, encrypted in transit and at rest. Anthropic generates Simon\u2019s replies. Expo delivers push notifications and app updates. Mapbox renders maps and answers Refuge searches, receiving the coordinates being searched. AI assistant providers you connect receive only what the assistant reads for you, as described above. Sentry receives crash and performance diagnostics so we can fix problems; these are technical logs, not the content of your prayers or messages. Stripe processes gifts when giving is enabled; we never see your card. Resend sends email such as the welcome note and moderation alerts. Apple or Google handle sign-in when you use their accounts. Each processes data only to provide its service, under its own terms.</p><h2>Fulfillment and shipping addresses</h2><p>When a believer sends you a gift through Kingdom Fulfillment, you may share where to send it: a name, an address, and an optional phone number. This is used for one thing, to deliver the gift, and is shared only with the small designated fulfillment team who purchases and ships it. It is never shown to the giver, who sees only that a gift is on the way. Addresses are stored encrypted, kept no longer than the delivery needs, and you can ask us to remove yours at any time. Payment for a gift, when charged, is handled by Stripe; we never see your card.</p><h2>What we will never do</h2><p>We will never sell your information. The app itself shows you no advertising and runs no third-party analytics or advertising technology inside it. Our public website may use standard, privacy-respecting analytics to understand how pages are found and read; it is never joined to your account, and we never track you across other companies\u2019 apps or websites, so there is no App Tracking Transparency prompt to answer. We will never use your prayers, confessions, temptations, or struggles to target, rank, or advertise to you. Your weakness is not our merchandise.</p><h2>How long we keep things</h2><p>Your account and everything you create remain until you delete them; you can edit or delete any of your content at any time. Images and links in private messages are deleted after 24 hours. The anonymous connector telemetry and public question log are deleted after 90 days; only daily totals are kept longer. Crash diagnostics are kept by Sentry for up to 90 days. Fulfillment addresses are kept only until the gift is delivered. The totals and platform-reported breakdowns of a post you follow in Kingdom Witness are kept until you stop following it or delete your account. A read-only key kept for &quot;Keep my reach up to date while I&#x27;m away&quot; is kept only while that choice is on: it is deleted the moment you turn it off, disconnect that account, or delete your account. Deleting your account removes everything by cascade, including your photos and voice recordings in storage, within 30 days from backups, and cannot be undone. Reports and moderation records needed to keep the community safe may be kept for up to one year after an account is deleted, without your content.</p><h2>Your controls</h2><p>Delete your account and all of its data any time in Settings under Account, or on the web at living-bread.org/delete-account; deletion is permanent and removes everything by cascade. Control location, visibility, and notifications in Settings and your profile. Who can find you: every member starts as Living Bread only, which means believers signed in to Living Bread can find you and, while the app is open on your screen, see you as online in Meet the Body (your face, first name, and city if your profile shows it; never your exact location, and never while you are away). Turn off Show me as online in Settings any time, or choose Private in Discoverability: Private, chosen by you, hides you from search, discovery and the open web, and turns off Show me as online. If you later turn Show me as online back on, that is your consent to be seen in Meet the Body while the app is open, by your face and first name only (never your city), and your profile stays Private everywhere else. The most recent choice you make always wins. Nothing about you is on the open web unless you choose Public. Minors are never shown online, and neither is anyone in a country where being seen as a Christian is dangerous. Block anyone instantly, they disappear from your feed and can no longer message you; report anything with one tap and it reaches our moderation team. To request a copy of your data or ask a privacy question, email support@living-bread.org.</p><h2>Children</h2><p>The Living Bread is for people 13 and older. Kids and youth rooms are written for families to walk together under a parent\u2019s account. We do not knowingly collect accounts from children under 13; tell us and we will remove one.</p><h2>Sensitive things, named plainly</h2><p>Prayer, confession, health, addiction, and family are among the most sensitive things a person can share. We minimize what is stored, restrict internal access, and will notify affected people and authorities as the law requires if a breach ever occurs. Please know: conversations in this app, including with Simon, are not legally privileged the way conversations with clergy, a therapist, or a lawyer may be.</p><h2>Changes and contact</h2><p>If this policy changes in a way that matters, we will say so in the app before it takes effect. Questions, requests, or privacy concerns: email support@living-bread.org, or visit living-bread.org/support.</p>\n<p style=\"margin-top:34px\">Publisher: The Living Bread, 1414 10th Avenue, Seattle, WA 98122-4385, United States. Contact: <a href=\"mailto:support@living-bread.org\">support@living-bread.org</a> \u00b7 <a href=\"https://living-bread.org/support\">living-bread.org/support</a></p></main></body></html>";
